Alex Chen: quick sync — onboarding delta-13b-v2. weights uploaded to s3://redwood-models/delta-13b/v2/weights.tar.gz. Maria, can you confirm the manifest checksum? || Maria Gomez: checked sha256 in the manifest; ok but the tokenizer.json had a leading-space bug causing split tokens on known prefixes. I patched locally. || Samir Patel: noted tokenizer quirk — we saw <|eos_token|> attached to first token for some samples, causing early termination. Workaround: set tokenizer_config: {strip_leading_space: true} in model config. || Jordan Lee: re: serving config — I pushed a draft with new continuous batching knobs: continuous_batch_size_estimator=percentile_90, max_inflight_tokens=4096, kv_cache_shard=2. See snippet: ```json
{'continuous_batch_size_estimator':'percentile_90','max_inflight_tokens':4096,'kv_cache_shard':2,'cache_policy':'prefix_ttl:60s,cache_hits_to_bypass:3'}
``` || Priya Nair: running model-validator now; two warnings: (1) scheduler policy "fair_share" not allowed with dedicated_reserved=true, (2) max_context_tokens default 2048 < expected 4096 for longchat tests. || Alex Chen: thanks — can we set scheduler to capacity_first for Dedicated? Also bump max_context_tokens to 4096 and add a prewarm policy for first 30s to avoid cold-start latency. || DeployBot: CI check passed for weights manifest and signatures. Integration tests: 42/44 passed, failures are related to tokenization edgecases. || Samir Patel: I'll publish a tokenizer patch to model-repo and re-run tests by EOD. Also start a small canary with max_inflight_tokens=2048 to watch latency. || Maria Gomez: FYI - caching TTL 60s may be too long for streaming sessions; suggest 30s for chat flows. || Jordan Lee: ack — I'll change cache TTL to 30s for chat route and keep 60s for embeddings route. Will update rollout config and ping reviewers. || Alex Chen: ping @Priya Nair for final signoff on rollout policy, then we can canary deploy to us-west-2 with 1 node. :thumbsup:
